# Messages.
# Format: see data/README.md. Fields:
#   sort:                    sort key (editorial, not used by the program)
#   id:                      message id, used by the program
#   error:                   title of an error message (shown in red)
#   error-revised:           revised error title (not used by the program)
#   info:                    title of an information message (shown in gold)
#   info-revised:            revised info title (not used by the program)
#   text:                    message text; \n is a line break, \l toggles symbol translation, <param> is replaced
#   description:             when the message appears (for the programmer)
#   programmer-note:         comment to the programmer
#   buttons:                 buttons: 'Label:action.Label:action;default-index'

# Instructions for the creation of this file.  Copy the Excel material and paste into this file.  [The following resizing is unnecessary.]  Pull the borders of the table to make them appropriately wide.  Save as Text.
# `s terminates the sort field, used to resort messages according to various criteria.
# `n terminates the message name or message ID
# `d terminates the description of the source for the error (explanation by the programmer)
# `p terminates a comment to the programmer.
# `e terminates the error message (displayed in red by the program)
# `E terminates a revised version of the error message
# `i terminates the information message (displayed in gold by the program)
# `I terminates a revised version of the information message
# `x terminates the explanation (explanation for the user)
# Only one of `e or `i should appear for any message
# Blanks at the start and end of strings are trimmed
# \n forces a carriage return within the text.
# \l toggles conversion of Maggie-talk.  Default is OFF.
# Sort#  `s     Name or ID  `n     Present_Message  P_M_Term     New_Message  N_M_Term     Comment to Programmer  `p     Explanation  `x     Description  `d
sort: 01
id: TruErr001
text: At least one of the trees has an error in it.\nA red button indicates an erroneous tree.

sort: 02
id: TruErr002
text: At least one of the required trees is incomplete.\nA '?' button indicates an incomplete tree.

sort: 03
id: TruErr003
text: You must answer 'yes' or 'no' to the question.

sort: 04
id: TruErr004
text: To show an argument valid, none of the rows\nshould be checked.

sort: 05
id: TruErr005
text: For an argument to be valid, none\nof its rows can have all premises\ntrue and the conclusion false.

sort: 06
id: TruErr006
text: To show an argument invalid, you must check a row in \nwhich all premises are true, and the conclusion is false.

sort: 07
id: TruErr007
text: The row you have checked is incomplete.  You \nmust complete any tree indicated by a '?' button.

sort: 08
id: TruErr008
text: The row you have checked is not one in which \n all premises are true, and the conclusion false.

sort: 09
id: TruErr009
text: The expression <expression> is not a well formed formula.

sort: 10
id: TruErr010
text: That argument has no conclusion.

sort: 11
id: TruErr011
text: Some of the boxes marked with a 'T' or 'F' are wrong.

sort: 12
id: TruErr012
text: All of the boxes with a '?' need to be marked 'T' or 'F'.

sort: 13
id: TruErr013
text: You need to choose the correct number of rows for the truth table.

sort: 14
id: TruErr014
text: You need to press the OK button on the Setup panel to continue.

sort: 15
id: TruErr015
text: The number of sentence letters is not correct.  \nRemember to separate Sentence Letters with a period.

sort: 16
id: TruErr016
text: Could not parse <unparsed>.

sort: 17
id: TruErr017
text: <sentence> is not a sentence letter \nrelevant to this problem.

sort: 18
id: TruErr018
text: <sentence> has been used more than once.

sort: 19
id: TruErr019
text: The number of rows is not correct.  \nThe correct number is 2 to the power n, \nwhere n is the number of distinct atomic \nformulas (here, sentence letters).

sort: 20
id: TruErr020
text: The setup table needs to be completed.
